      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The board is not overstepping; it is acting as a necessary shield against the very real, measurable financial risks of being left behind in a market that now rewards social progress. You are correct that short-term friction exists, but ignoring the \"S\" in ESG is a strategic error that invites regulatory crackdowns, capital flight, and reputational damage that will eventually crush profitability far more than any temporary productivity dip. The investors who fear this are betting on a world where social signaling is irrelevant, but the data shows that in the modern economy, failing to align with these norms is a direct threat to long-term shareholder value.",
      "source": "target",
